{"kind":"table","sheet":"CTF stages","address":"A1:E17","rows":17,"cols":5,"values":[[null,null,null,null,null],["CTF scanning and follow-on stages",null,null,null,null],["Status reviewed","2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z",null,null,null],["Follow the relevant branches. Status describes project integration; planned/proposed work is not a delivery commitment.",null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],["Stage","Question","Tools","When to run","Built or planned"],["1. Discovery","What ports and protocols are reachable?","Nmap TCP/UDP; optional arp-scan locally","At the beginning; repeat selectively when coverage is incomplete","Partly built. TCP discovery works. Profiler UDP and local ARP integration are planned."],["2. Identification","What is actually running?","Nmap service detection, fingerprintx, curl/httpx, WhatWeb, certificate and SSH-key collection","As soon as discovery finds services","Partly built. Nmap, curl, WhatWeb, certificate/key collection and classification work. fingerprintx/httpx remain planned."],["3. Enumeration","What does each service expose?","Katana, ffuf, enum4linux-ng, LDAP/RPC/NFS/SNMP checks, testssl.sh","Once the relevant protocol is identified","Partly built. SMB/TLS profiling and Legion protocol actions exist. Crawling, ffuf and wider profiler coverage are planned."],["4. Focused assessment","Which weaknesses are plausible?","Selected Nuclei templates, WPScan, ZAP, product-specific checks","Once application, version, configuration or endpoint evidence provides a direction","Partly built. Legion has selected protocol-check actions. Nuclei, WPScan and ZAP integration are planned."],["5. Validation","Does the suspected weakness actually exist?","Manual requests, Burp/ZAP, appropriate individual checks","For specific promising findings","Partly built. Some protocol-test actions exist. A general finding-validation workflow and web-check integrations are planned."],["6. Exploitation / initial access","Can this weakness or recovered credential give us useful access?","Metasploit, sqlmap, Burp, selected Impacket tools, SSH or application clients","Once validation identifies a promising route or suitable credentials become available","Planned. Profiler Metasploit import works; it does not select exploits or establish access. The access handoff remains to build."],["7. Post-access enumeration","What can this account access, and what new opportunities are visible?","Native Linux commands, PowerShell, filesystem exploration, linPEAS/winPEAS","After obtaining access; repeat when the account, privileges or target changes","Planned. An integrated post-access enumeration stage is not built."],["8. Artifact and credential analysis","Do these files contain flags, passwords, keys, hashes or further clues?","File viewers, Cipher Watch, Hash Watch, John the Ripper, Hashcat","Whenever useful files or data become available, including before initial access","Built separately. Cipher Watch and Hash Watch work. File intake, target attribution and credential handoffs remain planned."],["9. Privilege escalation","Do we need greater permissions to reach the objective?","linPEAS/winPEAS for leads; manual checks and a suitable exploit or misconfiguration technique","When current permissions block the objective and enumeration reveals a plausible escalation path","Proposed. An escalation workflow is not built; detailed implementation scope is undecided."],["10. Pivoting / lateral movement","Can this access help us reach another challenge service, account or machine?","SSH tunnelling, Ligolo-ng, NetExec, selected Impacket tools","For multi-host challenges when another in-scope target is needed; restart discovery and enumeration there","Proposed. An integrated pivoting/lateral-movement workflow is not built; detailed scope is undecided."],["11. Flag recovery and submission","Have we obtained the challenge's required proof?","File/database clients, browser, decoding tools, competition submission page","As soon as a flag is accessible; submit it and check platform acceptance","Proposed. Decoding components exist. Integrated flag verification, tracking and submission remain to build."]]}
